        "original_id": "d67bd11d-a7ee-572c-8500-9c5cdaf8bd46",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Anemopaegma, Pithecoctenium, Bignonia, Bignoniaceae\n- Mythology: Semele, Dionysus, Zeus, Cadmus, Harmonia\n- People: Diogenes of Athens\n- Works: Semele, Achilles, Helen, Herakles, Thyestes, Medea, Oedipus, Chrysippus\n- Sources: Suda\n\nFacts:\n- Anemopaegma is a genus of flowering plants in the family Bignoniaceae.\n- In Greek mythology, Semele was the daughter of Cadmus and Harmonia.\n- In Greek mythology, Semele was the mortal mother of Dionysus by Zeus.\n- Pithecoctenium is a genus closely related to Bignonia and Anemopaegma.\n- The Suda lists the works of Diogenes of Athens as Semele, Achilles, Helen, Herakles, Thyestes, Medea, Oedipus, and Chrysippus.",
